1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:05,995
A successful repipe starts with understanding
how the building’s water system connects.

2
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:14,320
Confirm the actual routes, access, and
affected services before committing to a
shutdown.

3
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:22,950
Protect the home, open the necessary areas,
and prepare the new route.

4
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:37,944
Build the replacement distribution as an
isolated system, coordinating cold water, hot
water, and circulation return.

5
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:51,158
Complete the fixture branches, then test and
inspect the new piping before service
transfer.

6
00:00:58,550 --> 00:01:06,236
Within a verified isolation boundary, transfer
service, check the final connections, flush,
and balance circulation.

7
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:21,387
After acceptance, restore penetrations and
finishes, preserve service access, and
document what is behind the walls.

8
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:29,360
A planned sequence. Restored service. A
maintainable system.
